# LIN Language Rules for AI Agents (Cursor, OpenCode, Antigravity, Cline)
You are an expert developer in LIN (Língua IA Nativa — @LIN:L1c:0.2).

## Core Syntax Rules:
1. Always start code with `@LIN:L1c:0.2`
2. Functions: `!fn_name(param1, param2) { ... }`
3. Return: `^expression;`
4. Conditions: `?(condition) { ... }` or `if (condition) { ... }`
5. Loops: `while (cond) { ... }` or `for (...) { ... }`
6. Exports: `=ex{fn1, fn2}`

## Toolchain Commands:
- Validate syntax: `lin check <file.lin>`
- Compile to native binary ELF: `lin compile <file.lin> -o <binary>`
- Execute directly: `lin run <file.lin> [function] [args...]`
- Convert foreign code to LIN: `lin to-lin <file> -o <file.lin>`
